// `exists` driving a `forbid` (the deny path — all prior exists cases were
// `permit`). Read is permitted unconditionally, but forbidden whenever some
// user has logged in within the window. Since a forbid overrides a permit,
// the effective decision is: permit Read only when NO login precedes it.
// This exercises `exists` inside a `forbid` rule and the permit/forbid
// interaction.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
);

forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (u: String). formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: u }};
